  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental balances use the Total Governmental Funds column (p4): 'cash' balances are total fund balances (cash 358,070 + investments 26,867 + due from other governments 22,700 at year end), beginning 335,782 as printed. Gov statement of revenues is p4; business-type from proprietary statement of revenues, expenses and changes in net position (p6, total proprietary funds). Business-type measure is net position; roll-forward 962,724 + 967,671 - 935,057 - 60,000 = 935,338. Business-type receipts have no single printed total, so operating revenue 934,542 + non-operating 33,129 were added (computed). Business-type disbursements include depreciation as printed. Governmental transfers in 60,000 = General 30,000 + Other governmental 30,000 (Police); matching 60,000 transfer out is from the Light Fund (business-type, transfers_net -60,000). Balance sheet: Statement of Net Position (p1) 2025 Total column; no liabilities printed. Detail lines are the budgetary comparison schedules (pp9-21, budget column = original & final); no other detail schedule exists, so no double counting; budget schedules are budgetary basis and their beginning balances differ from the statements (e.g. Light/Water/Sewer cash vs net position). TIF and Meter Deposit schedules print no total revenues/expenditures line, so no detail_totals for them. Capital outlay lines assumed equipment purchases. Read pages 1-21 of 21"
